                        "entry_id": "e5427d86-4f8f-3f52-8f03-b238f2ab0f5d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A public ball, typically a masquerade, popular in the 18th century."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4efbb57c-669b-48b2-9f4f-11403b2ad562",
                                "sense_id": "b00f6726-38f7-37e6-99fc-bf4564fa0874",
                                "text": "May 26, 1742, Horace Walpole, letter to Horace Mann\nThere are to be ridottos at guinea tickets."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbd670ef-f133-4b39-a1a6-cbbdccaecfc4",
                                "sense_id": "b00f6726-38f7-37e6-99fc-bf4564fa0874",
                                "text": "Night came, with that increase of gaiety which has always been night's peculiar privilege—perhaps on the principle of contrast. Monday, it was the ridotto; Tuesday, the opera; Wednesday, Ranelagh; Thursday, the play; Friday, a ball; Saturday, a rout, or else a little of all these blended together."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
